romanized_response:
HTTP status code 429 Too Many Requests ane daani artham emitante, server ki em rate limit undi, mee request aa limit ni cross chesindi ani. Idi ee kindha cheppina kaaranalalo edaina kaavachu:

1. Ee request chese code chala saarlu thakkuva time lo run ayyi undavachu, daanivalla rate limit cross ayyi untundi.

2. Website spam ani anumaaninche requests ni 429 status code tho reject chestundi. Idi antey user agent oka common browser kaakapothe ani artham kaavachu, idi konni websites use chese oka simple check. Dinni sariddadaniki, mee GET request ki "User-Agent" header ni ee vidhanga add cheyyochu:

```
const response = await axios.get('https://www.realestate.com.au/rent/in-sydney,+nsw/list-1', 
     { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'browser.version' }  }
);
```

Guruthunchukondi, meeru `"browser.version"` ni oka actual browser user agent string tho replace cheyyali. Ee code ye application lo run avutundo daanini batti, idi user agent spoofing ga consider cheyyabadavachu, idi konni countries lo leda organizations laws kindha (leda website terms of service kindha, ye website ni ee code access cheyyadaniki try chestundo) restricted ga undavachu.

3. Website em other reason valla rate limiting chestundi. Idi request oka proxy through chesi undavachu, aa case lo aa proxy yokka other users chala requests chesi undavachu, kaani idi jarige avakaasham takkuva.

4. Website anni requests ni reject chestundi enduku ante adi denial of service attack kindha undi. Idi kuda jarige avakaasham takkuva, endukante alanti attack kindha unna server yokka typical behavior emitante traffic ni oka non-existent server ki route cheyyadam, leda completely deny cheyyadam, valid response em ivvakapovadam. Ayithe, website oka HTTP status code tho respond chesinaa, adi ekkuva ga server error 503 Service Unavailable avutundi, idi server overload ayinappudu istharu.

response_en:
Yes, certainly! The issue you're encountering is because the string literals "fizzbuzz", "fizz", and "buzz" are temporary values, and you are trying to return a reference to them, which is not allowed because they will be dropped at the end of the scope, and the returned reference would be dangling.

You can fix this error by returning &'static str instead of &str. &'static str refers to string literals, which have a 'static lifetime, meaning they last for the duration of the program. Here's an updated version of your code:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Note that the last arm returns a &'static str that is created from a String using the Box::leak function, which takes ownership of a Box<T> and returns a pointer to its contents, effectively leaking it. This is safe because the returned pointer will last for the duration of the program, but it should be used with care as it will not be cleaned up automatically.

romanized_response:
Avunu, tappakunda! Meeru face avutunna issue enti ante, n.to_string() oka temporary value create chestundi, and meeru daani ki reference return cheyyadaniki try chestunnaru, adi allow cheyyabadadu endukante a temporary value scope end ayyaaka drop avutundi, and return chesina reference dangling avutundi.

Meeru ee error ni fix cheyyataniki &str badulu &'static str return cheyyochu. &'static str string literals ni refer chestundi, vaatiki 'static lifetime untundi, ante avi program duration antha untaayi. Idigo mee code yokka updated version:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Gamaninchandi, last arm Box::leak function use chesi String nundi create chesina &'static str return chestundi. Ee function Box<T> yokka ownership teesukoni, daani contents ki pointer return chestundi, basically daanini leak chestundi. Idi safe endukante return chesina pointer program duration antha untundi, kaani jagrattaga vaadaali endukante adi automatic ga clean up avvadu.

response_en:
Merge sort is a divide and conquer algorithm that works by recursively splitting the input array in half until the arrays are split into single elements. Then, the sorted arrays are merged back together in sorted order.

The key benefits of merge sort over a simpler algorithm like bubble sort are:

1. It is a stable sort that does not change the relative order of elements with equal keys.
2. It has an efficiency of O(n log n) time complexity, making it a relatively efficient algorithm even for large input sizes. Bubble sort, on the other hand, has a quadratic time complexity of O(n^2), making it very inefficient for larger inputs.
3. It is a generic algorithm that can sort any type of data for which a comparison function exists.

Here is a Rust implementation example:
```rust
fn merge_sort(vec: &mut [i32]) {
    if vec.len() < 2 {
        return;
    }

    let mid = vec.len() / 2;
    let (left, right) = vec.split_at_mut(mid);

    merge_sort(left);
    merge_sort(right);

    merge(left, right, vec);
}

fn merge(left: &mut [i32], right: &mut [i32], vec: &mut [i32]) {
    let mut i = 0;
    let mut j = 0;
    let mut k = 0;

    while i < left.len() && j < right.len() {
        if left[i] < right[j] {
            vec[k] = left[i];
            i += 1;
        } else {
            vec[k] = right[j];
            j += 1;
        }
        k += 1;
    }

    while i < left.len() {
        vec[k] = left[i];
        i += 1;
        k += 1;
    }

    while j < right.len() {
        vec[k] = right[j];
        j += 1;
        k += 1;
    }
}
```

romanized_response:
Merge sort ane di oka divide and conquer algorithm, idi input array ni recursively rendu halves ga split chestundi, arrays single elements ga split ayye varaku. Tarvata, aa sorted arrays ni sorted order lo malli together ga merge chestaru.

Bubble sort laanti simpler algorithm tho compare cheste, merge sort yokka key benefits ivi:

1. Idi oka stable sort, equal keys unna elements yokka relative order ni change cheyadu.
2. Dini time complexity O(n log n), anduvalla pedda input sizes ki kuda idi relatively efficient algorithm. Bubble sort ki, on the other hand, O(n^2) ane quadratic time complexity untundi, anduvalla pedda inputs ki idi chala inefficient.
3. Idi oka generic algorithm, comparison function unna any type of data ni sort cheyagaladu.

Ikkada oka Rust implementation example undi:
```rust
fn merge_sort(vec: &mut [i32]) {
